    "body": "## Overview\n\nThe cudagraph \"Assigning / modifying buffers\" check from #11596 raises on any `update` in Dynamo's residual bytecode, so it also rejects unrelated dict updates. This PR only flags `<module>._buffers.update`, which is what Dynamo emits for a buffer assigned during forward.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Transformers backend models whose config sets `is_causal` (e.g. Ettin / ModernBERT decoder) compile with cudagraphs again: Transformers' `is_causal` handling leaves `kwargs.update({'is_causal': ...})` in the residual bytecode.\n- Buffer assignment during forward is still rejected.\n- Needed by #61276, whose Ettin test hits this.\n\n## Validation\n\n`tests/compile/test_wrapper.py::test_cudagraph_buffer_assignment_check` covers both cases on CPU; the kwargs case fails without the fix.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/compile/test_wrapper.py\npytest tests/models/transformers/test_backend.py::test_output_head_transform  # with #61276\n```\n\nTests: `test_wrapper.py` passes (CPU and B200); with #61276, Ettin `test_output_head_transform` goes from failing to passing and all 58 `test_backend.py` tests pass on B200.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
